<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06GY">Example <span data-tag="06GY">9.4.1.12</span>.</a> Let $\kappa \trianglelefteq \lambda $ be regular cardinals, where $\lambda $ is uncountable. Then the $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \lambda }$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda }$ are $(\kappa ,\lambda )$-compactly generated. This follows by combining Proposition <a data-tag="067B" href="/tag/067B">9.4.1.11</a> with Variants <a data-tag="06FU" href="/tag/06FU">9.3.2.21</a> and <a data-tag="06FW" href="/tag/06FW">9.3.2.25</a>, respectively (together with Remark <a data-tag="068R" href="/tag/068R">9.3.2.23</a> in the special case $\kappa = \aleph _0$). </p>
